      "math_academy_id": "q-18244",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor",
      "problem": "Given that the minor of ${a}_{22}$ is $-70$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2k & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 11 & 9 & k+3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2k & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 11 & ∗ & k+3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${a}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2k & 6 \\\\ 11 & k+3\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2k & 6 \\\\ 11 & k+3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2k\\cdot (k+3)-11\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k-66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{22}$ is $-70$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+6k-66 & =-70 \\\\ 2{k}^{2}+6k+4 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k+2 & =0 \\\\ (k+1)(k+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=-2.$",
      "answer_fields": [
